film adaptations of video games are more  often than not  unsuccessful but there's hope on the  horizon here's a rundown of the new  mortal kombat trailer  and the small details that may have  slipped past you in the midst of its  ultra-violent glory  right off the bat the trailer for 2021's  mortal kombat  gives audiences a good look at one of  the property's most prolific  and popular entities sub-zero portrayed  here by joe taslim  throughout the trailer's run time  sub-zero gives everyone a bad day  naturally during his rampage sub-zero  utilizes his cryomancer abilities  freezing his opponents and using ice  based weaponry against them he even  creates an ice wall which gamers can  perform when they play a sub-zero in  mortal kombat 11.  one interesting thing to note about this  particular sub-zero incarnation  is that his real name is bihan a fact  that director  simon mcquoid revealed in his trailer  breakdown for ign  for long time players of the mortal  kombat video games the name bihar should  ring some bells  he was the first to take on the sub-zero  mantle bihan appeared under the frosty  alias only in the first mortal combat  game  where he quickly met his demise and  granted his younger brother kwai liang  the chance to follow in his footsteps  however bihan eventually rose from the  grave as the villainous wraith  noobs cybot and continues to wreak havoc  under this dark persona to this day  mother would be so proud  shifting gears away from an established  name in the mortal kombat universe the  film's trailer also introduces a fresh  face to spruce up the decades-old roster  of combatants  carl jung played by lewis tan is a down  on his luck yet  experienced cage fighter who's called to  join the legendary mortal kombat  tournament  courtesy of the mysterious dragon shaped  birth mark on his chest  cole is framed as the film's main  protagonist and only enters a  competition to protect his loved ones  making him mortal combats emotional core  mcquoid explained to ign why he and his  team felt the need to include kol young  in the mortal kombat reboot saying we  felt it was okay to bring in a new  character  given that mortal kombat has over the  years introduced new characters quite a  bit  he reassured everyone that cole doesn't  detract from the slew of legacy  characters mccoy also expanded on the  newcomer's function as a storytelling  device  and how it should affect viewers who  haven't stepped into the mortal kombat  world before  adding as cole learns the audience  learns and it helps us bring in those  fresh sets of ice  a long standing aspect of the mortal  kombat mythos there's a diverse range of  realms  and the frequent universe altering  conflicts between their inhabitants  locations like netherrealm chaos realm  earth realm  and more have hosted many of the canon's  brutal wars  and the upcoming film doesn't have any  desire to hide their existence  in the mortal kombat trailer fans catch  a brief glimpse of outworld  a realm governed by shao khan the  footage shows the character molina  walking through the land  appearing to be a realistic take on the  barren yet mountainous wasteland  gamers have come to recognize whether or  not any other realms will appear in  mortal kombat  is up for debates but it's surely a  possibility speaking to ign about what  went into bringing out world to life for  his mortal combat adaptation  mccoyd revealed that he quote wanted to  bring the realism and an authenticity  and the non-vfx feel to these unreal  worlds  to do so the director and his team  managed to find an area on earth  that fit the look and feel of the famous  fantasy location  the director explained he shot this in a  disused coal mine in the middle of  australia  he also cited how important it was to  express legitimacy of outworld's  aesthetic  and how surprisingly few digital  enhancements were needed to bring it to  life  for the majority of the mortal kombat  trailer franchise favorite sonia blade  provides narration over various clips  during her narration she brings up an  ancient legend about a tournament of  champions  that urges the selected participants to  fight in the name of mortal combat  in the games the event was created to  ensure outworld's power didn't grow too  strong  begging the questions it's a realm once  again threatening the sanctity of the  cosmos and if so who will bravely  attempt to stop it  to answer the first question the trailer  for 2021's mortal kombat provides a  couple of hints as to who could be  responsible for the takeover  outworld's ruler xiao khan isn't shown  in the flesh  but a statue of him makes a cameo in the  trailer beyond shao khan they're very  much alive shang tsun  accompanied by his forearms champion  goro is a logical pick  the soul-stealing warlock is no stranger  to stirring up trouble in the mk  universe  becoming one of its most nefarious  villains over the years  and know a taste of things to come of  course what would the forces of evil be  without the forces of good to oppose  them the trailer also features a handful  of other iconic mortal kombat characters  who will also join the fray to varying  degrees  about halfway through the mortal kombat  movie trailer earthrealm's champions are  introduced in small vignettes  accompanied by voiceovers  there's sonja blade liu kang jax and of  course kano  who has a long bitter rivalry with sonia  and is usually a villain in the mortal  kombat  universe this little baby brings back  memories now doesn't it  what you used it to knife your mother in  the back but in the forthcoming film  kano is now a sort of good guy kano  doesn't introduce himself like the  others do  instead sonia does the job in voice over  while viewers see footage of kano  shooting a red laser out of one of his  eyes it lasts for only a couple of  seconds  but kano's laser eye holds a lot of  weight in the mortal kombat world  in the games kano is usually depicted as  having a partial metal face plate  that covers one of his eyes he had the  face plate implanted at a cybernetic  enhancement  following an injury jax inflicted upon  him before the start of the mortal  kombat game series  and it's outfitted with an infrared  laser over his eye  allowing him to do some serious damage  when battling his opponents  the new movie version of kano doesn't  have the faceplate  but does have the laser eye which  suggests that this ability  didn't come about the same way plus  considering kano is also being portrayed  as an anti-hero in 2021's mortal kombat  film  it's even more unlikely that he gained  his laser beam shooting eye  after getting into a fight with jax fans  will just have to wait to see the movie  themselves  to learn what kano's new cinematic  backstory will be  maybe he and the good guys will all be  friends  [Music]  closer to the end of the film's trailer  luke yang is seen summoning balls of  fire to his hands  letting out a determined battle scream  before he slams his hand down  and lets a trail of fire snake its way  across the ground in front of him  until it grows into a massive flaming  dragon video game fans will recognize  this as a take on liu kang's dragon form  one of his signature moves in the  franchise immortal combat 11  it comes as a fatal blow which sees a  flaming dragon appear behind his  opponent  but more often luke yang himself morphs  into a giant dragon to finish off his  opponents  there have been several variations of  liu kyung's dragon bites fatality over  the years  from a simple green dragon that jumps  torsos to a black-scaled recreation  of the iconic mortal kombat symbol  itself whatever form this power takes on  the movie  one thing's for sure it's going to be  unique  in some of the mortal kombat trailers  most exciting moments we're treated to a  condensed version of hanzo hasashi's  metamorphosis into scorpion  he's first shown slinging around his  trusty kunai for the first time  taking out a horde of bad guys in the  woods the next time viewers see him he  is engulfed in his signature hellfire  and  darning his samurai inspired armor ready  for battle against his arch enemies  sub-zero  the trailer includes a snippet of their  clash including the utterance of  scorpion's most famous line  considering that is one of mk's tent  bowl figures getting scorpion right in  live action was of the utmost importance  to mccoyd  that included sticking the landing with  his origin and transformation  which the director hoped to chronicle  throughout the movie mccoy told ign  what i wanted to do was literally show  scorpion being born  and the ingredients and how he comes  about the director went on to discuss  the opening fight sequence featuring  hasashi  he described it as quote brutal and  nasty  and based on the clips from the trailer  that assessment isn't too far off  it's no secret that the mortal kombat  video games aren't for the faint of  heart  they're gory gruesome and sometimes  cringe-worthy and that reputation  doesn't come from simple side-scrolling  punches and kicks  fatalities moves unique to each  character that spotlight mutilating  match ending animations  are a bloody staple of the ip given  their cinematic nature  it should come as no surprise that  they're included in the upcoming mortal  kombat movie  mccoy told ign that fatalities were  always going to be a part of the movie  confirming that everyone involved in the  making of mortal kombat was on board  with their inclusion from the top down  even still he admitted there's certainly  restrictions on what you can do  and some of the restrictions are sort of  strange and surprising and some of them  are kind of obvious  the director noted that the goal was to  quote push it to the limit  but he didn't want to include such  graphic scenes without necessary context  or story weight to them  from fan favorite characters to  recognizable locales the mortal kombat  trailer has it all  if nothing else at least it gives  everyone multiple points to speculate on  in the weeks before  the film opens to the public check out  one of our newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about your  favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

